<item><title>Central African Republic and Chad talks stall over return of rebel leaders</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/central-african-republic-and-chad-talks-stall-over-return-9e8f41/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/central-african-republic-and-chad-talks-stall-over-return-9e8f41/</guid><category>Central African Republic</category><description>Bangui and N&apos;Djamena are negotiating the return of three rebel chiefs in Chad, but Wagner&apos;s stakes in a gold mine are among the obstacles.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:01:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" length="41097" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Bangui beef sellers hold unsold meat as prices drive customers away</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/bangui-beef-sellers-hold-unsold-meat-as-prices-drive-717ff2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/bangui-beef-sellers-hold-unsold-meat-as-prices-drive-717ff2/</guid><category>Central African Republic</category><description>Rising supply and transport costs have pushed prices beyond many families’ means, leaving cuts on market stalls for up to two days.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:00:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/bangui-beef-sellers-hold-unsold-meat-as-prices-drive-717ff2/share.jpg" length="44810" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/bangui-beef-sellers-hold-unsold-meat-as-prices-drive-717ff2/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Bangui power cuts persist as official touts Sakaï 2 solar project</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/bangui-power-cuts-persist-as-official-touts-sakai-2-solar-9e9c66/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/bangui-power-cuts-persist-as-official-touts-sakai-2-solar-9e9c66/</guid><category>Central African Republic</category><description>Maxime Balalou said the plant would double maximum capacity and serve 300 000 households, while outages continue across the capital.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:00:20 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" length="41097" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Six of nine Central African candidates pass regional teaching exam in Bangui</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/six-of-nine-central-african-candidates-pass-regional-b14be2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cf/six-of-nine-central-african-candidates-pass-regional-b14be2/</guid><category>Central African Republic</category><description>They were among 324 successful candidates from 368 who sat the competition, which covered health, pharmacy, dentistry and animal sciences.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:44:29 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" length="41097" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cf.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
